                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;">
          <table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="vertical-align: top;border-collapse: collapse;mso-table-lspace: 0;mso-table-rspace: 0;" width="100%">
            <tr>
              <td style="font-size: 0px;padding: 0px 40px 0px 40px;border-collapse: collapse;mso-table-lspace: 0;mso-table-rspace: 0;">
                <div style="font-family:Montserrat, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#010047;text-decoration:none;"><a href="https://airflow.apache.org/docs/" style="text-decoration:none;color:#010047;"><b>Airbyte becomes an official Airflow provider</b></a>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="font-size: 0px;padding: 0px 40px 0px 40px;border-collapse: collapse;mso-table-lspace: 0;mso-table-rspace: 0;">
              <div style="font-family:Montserrat, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#010047;">Thanks to <a href="https://github.com/marcosmarxm">@marcosmarxm</a>, Airbyte has been released in Airflow's last release. We're now featured as a package provider! You can now run Airbyte jobs from Airflow directly. This was the most requested feature in the last few months.</div>
            </td>
          </tr>
