                          <td valign="middle" width="30%" style="border-collapse: collapse;mso-table-lspace: 0pt;mso-table-rspace: 0pt;"><a href="https://towardsdatascience.com/modern-data-stack-which-place-for-spark-8e10365a8772">
                            <img src="https://uploads-ssl.webflow.com/605e01bc25f7e19a82e74788/61f8696c7bf2604d30194a97_spark-logo.png" alt="" style="width: 100%;max-width: 200px;height: auto;margin: auto;display: block;border-radius: 8px;vertical-align: top;box-shadow: 2px 2px 2px 0px #DFDFDF;border: 0;line-height: 100%;outline: none;text-decoration: none;-ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic;"></a>
                          </td>
                          <td valign="middle" width="70%" style="border-collapse: collapse;mso-table-lspace: 0pt;mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
                            <div style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:20px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;color:#010047;text-decoration:none;padding-left: 25px;"><a href="https://towardsdatascience.com/modern-data-stack-which-place-for-spark-8e10365a8772" style="text-decoration: none;color:#010047;"><b>Modern Data Stack: Which place for Spark?</b></a></div>
                            <div style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#010047;padding-left: 25px;padding-bottom: 5px;">Furcy shared some of the limits of SQL and how dbt and Spark can be both part of your data stack. Recently, data warehouses started adding support for a DataFrame API similar to pySpark.</div>
                            <a href="https://towardsdatascience.com/modern-data-stack-which-place-for-spark-8e10365a8772" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#625EFF;padding-left: 25px;"><b>Read it here >> </b></span></a>

