          </div></div>`,eU=`<div class="ab-community-newsletter-md-body">
<p><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/1761684918073-header-thumbnail-01k8p9n405j534rg6pe4r5swk1-41a73448bb.png" alt="Airbyte" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></p>
<p>Thanks for reading this installment of the Airbyte Newsletter! We have some incredibly exciting updates to share with you, including:</p>
<ul><li>The New Airbyte Plus Plan</li><li>Snowflake Destination Updates</li><li>Apache Polaris Support</li><li>MSSQL Speed Updates</li><li>Michel Tricot at Sifflet Signals</li></ul>
<p><a href="https://airbyte.com">Visit our Website</a></p>
<h2>Introducing Airbyte Plus</h2>
<p><a href="https://airbyte.com/blog/airbyte-plus"><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/69005b1978334fc9eabf0ff3-unnamed-4-3c31710ad6.png" alt="Introducing Airbyte Plus" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></a></p>
<p>Airbyte Plus is a new pricing plan designed for growing teams looking for core functionality with the predictability of annual pricing and accelerated support.</p>
<p>Plus is identical to the Standard plan but offers annual billing instead of monthly usage-based pricing, eliminating cost fluctuations and making it easier to plan data infrastructure budgets for the year.</p>
<p>The plan also includes accelerated support with prioritized response times, perfect for small and mid-sized teams running mission-critical data pipelines who need extra support at a reasonable price.</p>
<p>Same product, same features, just predictable costs and faster support when you need it.</p>
<p><a href="https://airbyte.com/blog/airbyte-plus">Learn more...</a></p>
<h2>Snowflake Destination: Now Faster and Cheaper</h2>
<p><a href="https://airbyte.com/blog/snowflake-destination-enhancements"><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/airbyte-plus-snowflake-v6-white-01k8rt3wm14mpjbfagxck8qsq7-9beea4ee7e.png" alt="Snowflake Destination" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></a></p>
<p>We just shipped major performance improvements to our Snowflake destination that deliver dramatic speed and cost benefits:</p>
<ul><li>Up to 10x faster syncs</li><li>Up to 95% cost reduction</li></ul>
<p>This massively improves scaling as time-sensitive pipelines and dashboards get dramatically faster refresh rates at a fraction of the cost. These optimization principles are being rolled out across other destinations to make data movement so fast and affordable that cost and latency stop being concerns.</p>
<p>Read the full <a href="https://airbyte.com/blog/snowflake-destination-enhancements">blog post</a>.</p>
<h2>Apache Polaris Support for S3 Data Lakes</h2>
<p><a href="https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/destinations/s3-data-lake#polaris"><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/apache-polaris-01k8rv1h2p3r92xcr1mst77fz9-fe840bc22c.png" alt="Apache Polaris Support" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></a></p>
<p>Airbyte now supports Apache Polaris catalog integration in its S3 Data Lake Destination, bringing open table format management directly into your data pipelines.</p>
<p>This means you can write data to S3 while automatically registering tables in Polaris, enabling seamless interoperability across your data lakehouse tools like Spark, Trino, and Flink.</p>
<p>For teams building modern data architectures, this eliminates the manual catalog management overhead and ensures your S3 data is immediately queryable and discoverable across your entire stack.</p>
<p><a href="https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/destinations/s3-data-lake#polaris">Read our docs.</a></p>
<h2>MSSQL Speed Updates</h2>
<p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/micheltricot_mssql-syncs-with-airbyte-just-got-84-faster-activity-7386802810035732480-lMHS"><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/airbyte-plus-mssql-01k8rtkm5c94zr5c11448mc6gd-e916f579e8.png" alt="MSSQL Speed Updates" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></a></p>
<p>Airbyte's MSSQL connector just got a massive performance upgrade, delivering 84% faster syncs after migrating to the new CDK with built-in speed mode. As Airbyte's third-largest database source by volume, SQL Server is now also one of their fastest connectors.</p>
<p>The enhancement is rolling out to customers soon. If you're syncing SQL Server data at scale, expect dramatically faster pipeline performance.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/micheltricot_mssql-syncs-with-airbyte-just-got-84-faster-activity-7386802810035732480-lMHS">Read our CEO's post on it here.</a></p>
<h2>Airbyte CEO Michel Tricot at Sifflet Signals</h2>
<p><a href="https://www.siffletdata.com/signals-2025"><img src="/images/community/newsletter/bodies/external/oct-2025-introducing-airbyte-plus/signals-michel-t-01k8rvvt6w4ph34mhcszc4ew9g-a83b1ddc1e.png" alt="Michel Tricot at Sifflet Signals" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></a></p>
<p>Airbyte CEO Michel Tricot is speaking at Signals Summit 2025 on November 19 about how sovereign data movement changes this equation.</p>
<p>The core challenge: AI agents need access to comprehensive, real-time data across your entire infrastructure. But traditional approaches force you to choose between AI capabilities and data control.</p>
<p>Michel will break down:</p>
<ul><li>How sovereign architectures let AI access data without exposing it</li><li>Maintaining security boundaries while enabling agent workflows</li><li>Meeting compliance requirements without blocking AI deployment</li></ul>
<p><a href="https://www.siffletdata.com/signals-2025">Register now!</a></p>
