                        <div style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:20px;line-height:1.3;text-align:left;color:#010047;text-decoration:none;padding-left: 25px;"><a href="https://medium.com/@mrtrustworthy/from-data-driven-to-driving-data-the-dysfunctions-of-data-engineering-34c34496ed8e" style="text-decoration: none;color:#010047;"><b>From Data Driven to Driving Data— The dysfunctions of Data Engineering</b></a></div>
                        <div style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#010047;padding-left: 25px;padding-bottom: 5px;">An article about what the dysfunctions of data engineering are. You'll find a lot of founding concepts in the article: type of data engineers, inversion of responsibility, driving data rather than data-driven.</div>
                        <a href="https://medium.com/@mrtrustworthy/from-data-driven-to-driving-data-the-dysfunctions-of-data-engineering-34c34496ed8e" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;color:#625EFF;padding-left: 25px;"><b>Check the ranking >> </b></span></a>

